ITEMS = [
    {"key":"C","correct":"A personal letter that uses a story to speak directly to a future reader","wrong":["A timetable listing public opening hours","A recipe that gives cooking instructions","A dictionary entry defining a single word"],"prompt":"Hey, Future Me,\nWhen I was nine, I planted a tiny tree with Grandpa. It leaned after the first storm, so we tied it to a stake. I hope you still visit that hill and remember how one careful afternoon changed an empty corner.\nLove, Jo\n\nWhich description best identifies this text?","strategy":"把稱呼、署名和直接對收信者說話的句子，與其中回憶事件的段落一起判斷體裁。","steps":["先看開頭 Hey, Future Me 和結尾 Love, Jo，辨認書信的稱呼與署名。","找出文中回憶的事件：和祖父種樹、暴風後扶正樹苗。","注意作者直接對未來的自己說話，因此它不只是第三人稱故事。","排除時刻表、食譜和字典條目，因為文本沒有相應欄位或定義格式。","選擇兼具書信形式與個人敘事內容的描述，並用稱呼及事件作證。"],"refs":[("nh112","第5頁閱讀題組(三)第53–55題：辨認寫給未來自己的信件對象與內容"),("yc114","第3頁閱讀題組第39–44題：由日記敘述者的個人經歷理解文本"),("kc111","第2頁閱讀題組第24–26題：依角色經歷與事件順序辨認敘事文本")]},
    {"key":"B","correct":"To explain how rainwater moves through soil and becomes groundwater","wrong":["To invite readers to a birthday celebration","To tell a fictional mystery about a missing dog","To persuade readers to buy a new pair of shoes"],"prompt":"Rain falls on the hills and enters small spaces between rocks and soil. Some water flows downhill into streams; some moves deeper until it reaches a layer that holds water. Wells can draw from this underground supply.\n\nWhat is the main purpose of this passage?","strategy":"從因果詞和過程先後判斷作者是在解釋現象，而不是講故事或提出行動邀請。","steps":["圈出 falls、enters、flows、moves、reaches、draw 等過程動詞。","依序整理雨水落下、滲入土壤、流向溪流或深入含水層的路徑。","辨認段落回答的是「地下水如何形成」，而非要求讀者採取某項行動。","排除生日邀請、失狗故事與商品推銷，因為文中沒有受邀者、角色衝突或購買資訊。","以連續的自然因果過程說明其主要目的為解釋地下水形成。"],"refs":[("nh113","第3頁閱讀題組A第27–34題：依說明段落的因果與資訊選擇理解重點"),("kc111","第3頁閱讀題組E第27–29題：依問題、影響與解決方式理解說明文"),("yc114","第3頁閱讀題組第39–44題：由連續事件和原因理解文本內容")]},
    {"key":"D","correct":"Tell eligible students when and where to attend and what to bring","wrong":["Describe the history of the school building","Narrate a character’s feelings about a friendship","Explain how a recipe changes when baked"],"prompt":"SCIENCE WALK — Saturday, May 18\nMeet at the east gate at 8:20 a.m. Bring a water bottle and a notebook. Students in Grades 7–9 may join. Sign up with Ms. Lin by Thursday.\n\nWhat should a reader mainly get from this notice?","strategy":"辨認通知的標題、時間地點、資格、攜帶物與報名方式，將資訊連回讀者要完成的行動。","steps":["看標題 SCIENCE WALK，辨認它公告的是一場活動。","找出日期、集合地點與時間，判斷參加者何時何地報到。","確認 Grades 7–9 的資格和須攜帶的兩樣物品。","讀 sign up by Thursday，找出報名對象與截止時間。","將公告目的概括成提供參加活動所需的時間、地點、資格與準備資訊。"],"refs":[("nh112","第4頁閱讀題組(一)第48–50題：依失物公告內容判斷讀者可採取的行動"),("yc114","第3頁閱讀題組第45–47題：從對話辨認安全通知的行動目的"),("kc108","第4頁閱讀題組E第34–36題：由廣告和對話理解訊息內容與目的")]},
    {"key":"A","correct":"A comparison table that lets readers match a day with its closing time","wrong":["A first-person story about a visitor’s vacation","A script with character names and spoken lines","A persuasive advertisement promising a discount"],"prompt":"The chart lists the museum’s hours:\nTue–Fri 9:00–17:00\nSaturday 9:00–19:00\nSunday 10:00–16:00\nClosed Monday\n\nWhich text form is most useful for finding Saturday’s closing time quickly?","strategy":"注意資料以日別和時間欄列呈現；表格的對齊結構適合快速查找對應資料。","steps":["觀察每個星期和時段各自成列，辨認資訊以表格形式排列。","把題目中的 Saturday 對應到同一列，而非跨列拼接時間。","沿著 Saturday 那列找到時間區間的右端 19:00。","確認題目問的是關門時間，不是開門時間或休館日。","判斷此資料最適合用比較表格呈現，因為讀者能按日別迅速查欄。"],"refs":[("kc111","第3頁閱讀題組F第30–32題：根據圖表欄列比較熱帶氣旋資料"),("nh112","第4頁閱讀題組(二)第51–52題：依開放時間與票價表格查詢資訊"),("kc109","第3頁閱讀題組第29–31題：整合表格／方案資料完成具體比較")]},
    {"key":"C","correct":"The writer is sending a personal message to someone they know","wrong":["The writer is listing rules for every library visitor","The writer is reporting an impersonal scientific experiment","The writer is advertising a product to all customers"],"prompt":"Dear Mei,\nI found the blue notebook you left in the art room. I put it in the front office, so you can pick it up after class. The paper birds we made are still hanging by the window. They make me smile whenever I pass.\nSee you, Anya\n\nWhat is the writer’s main purpose?","strategy":"從稱呼、代名詞、具體共同經驗和結尾判斷寫信對象及溝通目的。","steps":["讀 Dear Mei 確認訊息直接寫給一位特定收信人。","找出最需要傳達的事項：遺失的筆記本已送到辦公室。","辨認 art room 和共同做的紙鳥是兩人共享的情境細節。","區分主要功能和附帶的友善敘述；本文不是普遍規則或公開廣告。","概括作者是在告知朋友物品所在並分享一則個人近況。"],"refs":[("nh112","第5頁閱讀題組(三)第53–55題：分析私人信件的收信對象、內容與寫信目的"),("yc114","第3頁閱讀題組第39–44題：從私人日記內容理解作者的生活脈絡"),("kc108","第4頁閱讀題組E第34–36題：解讀交織對話與公開廣告的溝通目的")]},
    {"key":"B","correct":"A short drama script, because character labels and stage directions organize the scene","wrong":["A timetable, because it lists exact clock times","A recipe, because it names ingredients and cooking steps","A formal letter, because it has a greeting and signature"],"prompt":"(At the bus stop, Nia checks the dark sky.)\nNIA: The rain is getting stronger. Should we move the books inside?\nOMAR: Yes. I’ll carry the box while you call the library.\n(They hurry toward the school door.)\n\nWhich feature most clearly identifies this text form?","strategy":"用角色標籤、直接台詞與括號中的動作提示辨認短劇，不只看情境發生在哪裡。","steps":["檢查 NIA、OMAR 是否以角色名稱標出每段發話者。","辨認括號裡的動作提示，說明人物何時移動或做事。","觀察故事資訊主要透過角色對話和舞台動作展開。","排除時刻表、食譜和正式書信，因為它們不以角色輪流說話及舞台提示編排。","選擇短劇腳本，並用角色標籤與括號動作作體裁證據。"],"refs":[("yc114","第3頁閱讀題組第45–47題：由角色輪流說話的對話判斷交流情境"),("kc108","第4頁閱讀題組E第34–36題：透過角色對話解釋廣告內容"),("nh113","第2頁閱讀題組第21題：由對話輪替和說話目的辨認文本形式")]},
    {"key":"D","correct":"A persuasive advertisement that promotes a repair service and urges customers to call","wrong":["A neutral report presenting a controlled repair experiment","A diary entry recounting one person’s visit to a workshop","A public timetable listing the service’s weekly opening hours"],"prompt":"Tired of a wobbly chair? At Fix-It Saturday, volunteers can help you tighten a loose leg and learn a repair skill. Bring one small item to the community hall, 10 a.m.–noon. “The easiest way to give your things a second life!” Reserve a place today.\n\nWhich description best fits this text?","strategy":"檢查吸引注意的問句、正向宣稱和呼籲行動，辨識廣告的說服目的，也把可核實的活動資訊與宣稱分開。","steps":["注意開頭以讀者問題抓注意，接著說明服務能協助修理物品。","找出時間、地點和 Bring one small item 等參加資訊。","辨認 Reserve a place today 是促使讀者採取行動的呼籲。","把 easiest 等宣傳性評語視為廣告宣稱，不當成已證實的客觀比較。","判斷它是推廣修理服務並邀請報名的廣告，兼有具體活動安排。"],"refs":[("kc110","第3頁閱讀測驗第24–26題：從服務內容、優惠與呼籲辨認廣告目的"),("kc108","第4頁閱讀題組E第34–36題：讀取廣告宣稱並結合對話理解內容"),("kc111","第3頁閱讀題組E第27–29題：由問題、服務影響與建議辨認說服方式")]},
    {"key":"C","correct":"The chart supports comparing amounts by category, but it does not explain why they changed","wrong":["The chart proves why every household changed its habits","The chart is a fictional story with a narrator","The chart gives step-by-step instructions for sorting each item"],"prompt":"A recycling infographic shows paper collected: April 18 kg, May 24 kg, June 21 kg. Its caption says, “More neighbors are joining!”\n\nWhat can the chart itself support most directly?","strategy":"先分清數值圖表與圖說主張：圖表能顯示數量變化，不能單獨證明變化背後的原因。","steps":["讀標題或標籤，確認三個數值都代表每月回收紙張公斤數。","比較數字：五月比四月多，六月又比五月少。","辨認圖表直接提供的是分類數量與月份差異。","將 caption 的參與者增加視為另一項主張；單憑公斤數不能證明每戶都改變習慣。","選擇只描述圖表能支持的比較，並指出它本身不交代原因。"],"refs":[("kc111","第3頁閱讀題組F第30–32題：從表格直接比較數據並限制推論"),("kc109","第3頁閱讀題組第29–31題：依方案資料和數量欄完成比較"),("nh112","第4頁閱讀題組(二)第51–52題：從資訊表格擷取可直接確認的內容")]},
    {"key":"A","correct":"Check the material list, complete one action at a time, then use the warning to verify the safe result","wrong":["Treat the directions as a story and skip the order","Use the last step first, even if earlier steps are required","Follow the picture colors but ignore the written safety note"],"prompt":"HOW TO START A SEEDLING\n1. Fill a small pot with damp soil.\n2. Place one seed near the surface and cover it lightly.\n3. Set the pot by a bright window.\n4. Water when the top soil feels dry.\nNote: Do not leave the pot in standing water.\n\nHow should a reader use this text?","strategy":"程序說明依序列出可執行步驟，並用注意事項限制操作；閱讀時要保留順序與條件。","steps":["辨認 HOW TO 標題和編號，確認這是程序／操作說明。","按 1 到 4 整理裝土、播種、放置和後續澆水的順序。","注意第四步含 when the top soil feels dry 的條件，不是固定每天澆水。","把末尾警告連回澆水行動，避免讓盆栽長時間泡水。","依序照做並以安全註記檢查結果，而不是跳步或忽略限制。"],"refs":[("kc113","第6頁閱讀題組第33–35題：依咖啡製作說明判斷步驟順序與內容"),("kc108","閱讀題組B第21–25題：依鬆餅食譜的連接詞、材料與步驟理解程序"),("nh112","第4頁閱讀題組(一)第48–50題：依公告指示判斷讀者可採取的行動")]},
    {"key":"B","correct":"Use the explanation for why, the table for when, and the notice for what action to take","wrong":["Treat all three sections as one fictional story","Use only the table to explain why recycling matters","Ignore the notice because a webpage should contain only one genre"],"prompt":"A town webpage has three parts: a short paragraph explains why batteries should not go in regular trash; a calendar lists collection dates; a notice says to place used batteries in a sealed box at the library desk.\n\nHow should a reader use these different parts?","strategy":"逐區辨認文本功能，再依任務問題選用相應資料；同一頁面可以把數種體裁組合起來。","steps":["把說明段落、日期表和公告分別標記為原因資訊、時間資料及操作指示。","如果想知道為何分類，回到說明段落找環境或安全理由。","如果要安排送交時間，查日期表而非從說明文猜測。","如果已準備好電池，依公告到圖書館服務台並使用密封盒。","將三種資訊分工整合，避免把表格當原因或忽略行動規則。"],"refs":[("kc111","第3頁閱讀題組F第30–32題：圖表回答數據比較，不代替說明文的原因"),("nh112","第4頁閱讀題組(二)第51–52題：時間表和公告註記各自提供不同資訊"),("kc109","第3頁閱讀題組第29–31題：整合圖表條件與附帶說明作決策")]},
]

KEYS = "CBDACBDACB"
all_steps, all_strategies, failures = [], [], []
for i, item in enumerate(ITEMS, 1):
    path = QROOT / f"question-english-performance-3-iv-16-{i}.json"
    data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    key = KEYS[i - 1]
    pos = ord(key) - 65
    distractors = item["wrong"]
    arranged = distractors[:pos] + [item["correct"]] + distractors[pos:]
    data["prompt"] = item["prompt"]
    data["options"] = [{"id": letter, "text": text} for letter, text in zip("ABCD", arranged)]
    data["answer"] = {"value": key, "explanation": f"正解{key}：{item['strategy']}"}
    data["solutionStrategy"] = item["strategy"]
    data["solutionSteps"] = item["steps"]
    data["reviewStatus"] = "draft"
    refs = []
    for source_key, locator in item["refs"]:
        url, title, year = SOURCES[source_key]
        refs.append({"url": url, "title": title, "year": year, "subject": "english", "locator": locator, "locatorLevel": "item", "observedPattern": "僅取公立學校英文公開評量的體裁辨認、目的判讀、結構閱讀或資料推理能力模式；此題文本、情境、選項與答案均重新創作。", "reuseDecision": "pattern-only", "status": "recorded"})
    data["examPatternRefs"] = refs
    data["provenance"] = {"origin":"original","license":"All rights reserved","sourceUrl":refs[0]["url"],"sourceLocator":"參照內湖國中112-1七年級Q48–55、113-2八年級Q21及Q27–40、鹽埕國中114-2九年級Q39–47、國昌國中108-2七年級Q21–25及Q34–36、110-2八年級Q24–26、111-2八年級Q27–32、109-1八年級Q29–35及113-2七年級Q33–35的不同體裁與題型；逐題 locator 見 examPatternRefs。","authoringNote":"所有英文文本、題幹、選項、答案與解析均為原創；公開試卷僅提供可追溯的題型能力模式參照；狀態維持draft。"}
    path.write_text(json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    all_steps.extend(item["steps"])
    all_strategies.append(item["strategy"])
    if data["options"][pos]["text"] != item["correct"] or len(set(item["steps"])) != 5 or len(refs) != 3:
        failures.append(path.name)
if len(set(all_steps)) != 50: failures.append("reused-solution-steps")
if len(set(all_strategies)) != 10: failures.append("reused-strategies")
report = {"unit":"3-Ⅳ-16","checked":10,"passed":10 if not failures else 10-len(failures),"uniqueStrategies":len(set(all_strategies)),"uniqueSolutionSteps":len(set(all_steps)),"failures":failures,"status":"pass" if not failures else "fail","notes":"十題涵蓋書信、敘事、說明文、通知、表格、對話／短劇、廣告、資訊圖表、程序說明與混合網頁；每題有原創文本、正解、繁中解析、專屬策略、五步詳解及三筆精確題號公校試題pattern-only來源，全部維持draft。"}
(ROOT / "implementation/reports/english-performance-3-iv-16-first-pass-review.json").write_text(json.dumps(report, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
print(json.dumps(report, ensure_ascii=False))
raise SystemExit(bool(failures))
